<title>GERMANY: Volksfuersorge sees good 1997 earnings.</title>
<headline>Volksfuersorge sees good 1997 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurance group Volksfuersorge AG, a unit of AMB Holding, said on Tuesday it expected moderate growth and a good profit in 1997.</p>
<p>Chief executive Hans Jaeger told the company's shareholder meeting new life insurance business had risen in the first five months of the year and claims had dropped both in life and non-life segments.</p>
<p>In non-life lines, new business rose by 27.5 percent, or 184,000 contracts through the end of May.</p>
<p>However gross premiums had dropped by two percent to 621 million marks from the year-ago period.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
